# Temperance marker — cli#506
- date: 2026-11-08
- branch: fix/506-trust-window-spent-on-publish
- scope-decision: teach the trust window to close when the publish it paid for
  lands. One query, one new test inside `trust_window_closed`, and a reason
  string so callers can say why a window reads closed.
- smallest shape: the fix is a read, not a write. The marker is local and the
  publish is remote, so no write was ever possible.
- what this does NOT do: nothing fires `rearm` on a schedule. That is still
  #488's open item. This makes the trigger worth more, it does not supply one.
- blast radius: `scripts/publish-gate.sh` only, which is not in dist/lite, so
  no adopter reads it. Every new path leans toward "approval required".
- drift-trigger: if the fix needs the workflow to write anything, stop — that
  is the impossible shape the diagnosis ruled out.
